<title>SWITZERLAND: First Swiss beet tests show mixed sugar content.</title>
<headline>First Swiss beet tests show mixed sugar content.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's first sugar beet tests showed mixed average sugar content compared with last year, Zuckerfabriken Aarberg und Frauenfeld AG said.</p>
<p>The results were presented from two refineries following a merger of Aarberg and Frauenfeld operations. The report omits beet weight. The test was conducted July 30. Details follow -</p>
<p>				 1st test 97  1st test 96   Avg 92-96</p>
<p>Refinery Aarberg:</p>
<p> Beet yield 1)		42.0	  50.1	    39.0</p>
<p> Leaf-root weight ratio   1.4	   1.2	     1.2</p>
<p> Sugar content, percent   14.2	  16.0	    14.6</p>
<p> Sugar yield 2)	     6,065	 8,016	   5,721</p>
<p> Rain since April 1 (mm)  423.9	 253.4	   340.1</p>
<p>Refinery Frauenfeld:</p>
<p> Beet yield 1)		47.5	  60.4	    50.1</p>
<p> Leaf-root weight ratio   1.2	   1.2	     1.1</p>
<p> Sugar content, percent   14.9	  13.8	    14.6</p>
<p> Sugar yield 2)	     7,054	 8,347	   7,261</p>
<p> Rain since April 1 (mm)  387.1	 462.0	   518.2</p>
<p>1) tonnes per hectare</p>
<p>2) kilogram per hectare</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
